# class: stair-safety
# origin: audits/2026-10-18-first-contact.md T1 (first-contact-plans/5-townhouse.arch L0: stair st entered at y 9600,
#   275 mm from the front wall face, with no landing; the g_front swing covers the only floor there; reduced with the
#   front door in front of the foot, and the flight 800 mm wide and 2700 long so its foot keeps a landing: T1's
#   second defect, the missing landing, is foot-against-partition's case)
# expect: W_SWING_OVER_STAIR
# status: done
# fact: st (x 150-950, y 200-2900, dir up) is entered at its south end y 2900, 975 mm before the shell's inner face at
#   y 3875 (a landing for an 800 mm flight). d_front (x 300-1100) is hinged at (300,4000) and swings in with an 800 mm
#   leaf, sweeping x 300-1100, y 3200-4000: into the 400 mm a door must leave clear beyond the bottom step (y 2900-3300)
plan "Front door swinging at the foot of the stair" {
  units mm
  grid 50
  wall id=shell exterior thickness 250 { (0,0) (5500,0) (5500,4000) (0,4000) close }
  wall id=w_v partition thickness 100 { (2200,0) (2200,4000) }
  room id=r_hall at (0,0) size 2200x4000 label "Hall" uses hall
  room id=r_liv at (2200,0) size 3300x4000 label "Living" uses living
  door id=d_front at (700,4000) width 800 wall shell hinge near end swing into r_hall
  door id=d_liv at (2200,1500) width 900 wall w_v swing into r_liv
  window at (3800,4000) width 1800 wall shell
  window at (3800,0) width 1800 wall shell
  stair id=st at (150,200) size 800x2700 dir up
}
